# Has anybody tested the model's central assumption? One row per answer, with how many stacks
# gave it.
#
# The most important number here
#   It is the single most important number in this repository, and a bare coupling list cannot
#   carry it. This model assumes layers hold their remainders independently, `C = 0`. The schema's
#   own annotation says a document with no couplings "is not evidence of independence; it is a
#   document where nobody looked", and an empty list has no column that says which.
#
# What the corpus answers
#   Some stacks file couplings, some say nobody looked, a single-layer stack has no pair to
#   couple, and none says somebody looked and found independence. The central assumption has
#   never been confirmed and has been contradicted.
#
# Corpus only, and the fixture is why
#   `every-absence.xml` asserts independence on purpose, to prove the branch works. Counting a
#   stipulation here would answer "has anybody tested this?" with a yes that nobody earned, which
#   would turn the finding into a lie.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings/pm:absent, over the corpus.
SELECT CASE
         WHEN s.answer IS NULL              THEN 'somebody looked and the layers MOVE TOGETHER'
         WHEN s.answer = 'none'             THEN 'somebody looked and found independence'
         WHEN s.answer = 'notApplicable'    THEN 'one layer; no pair to couple'
         ELSE 'NOBODY LOOKED'
       END AS the_independence_assumption,
       count(*) AS stacks
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) s
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
) c USING (filing)
GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
